Track 3: Phase Distortion Ritual
- Story & Context: The communal gathering in the central chamber of the old plant, a space they now called "The Kiln," began with the low thrum of the 8-string guitar, vibrating through the massive concrete floor as the collective prepared to commune, their faces illuminated by the projected fractal patterns. A sudden, violent feedback loop erupted from the central modular rig, a deliberate sonic offering designed to strip away the mundane and connect them to the vast, cold emptiness of the cosmos, transforming their shared anxiety into a strange, defiant unity. "We are the signal, we are the receiver," chanted the crowd, their voices merging with the distorted frequencies, acknowledging their place in the brutalist tapestry of existence.
